    {
      "id": 16,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "KV Cache Hit Rate (prefix cache)",
      "description": "REQUIRED by Phase 4 goal. vLLM v0.25.1 exposes prefix-cache hits/queries as Counters named vllm:prefix_cache_hits / vllm:prefix_cache_queries in source (vllm/v1/metrics/loggers.py); the prometheus_client library auto-appends '_total' to every Counter at scrape time, so the real series names on the wire are vllm:prefix_cache_hits_total and vllm:prefix_cache_queries_total -- confirmed by reading both the pinned v0.25.1 source and the prometheus_client Counter implementation, not assumed. This is vLLM's native prefix-cache hit rate, which is the mechanism SPEC.md's 'KV cache hit rate' metric refers to on this build -- no custom exporter needed.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
